# Merged after halium.config, which reorders CONFIG_LSM to put apparmor ahead of
# selinux. Only one LSM_FLAG_EXCLUSIVE module initialises (prepare_lsm() in
# security/security.c skips the rest), so that ordering silently disables
# SELinux: the kernel logs "AppArmor initialized" and never "SELinux:
# Initializing", and /sys/fs/selinux does not exist.
#
# mayfly's stock /vendor/bin/vndservicemanager is the Android 12+ C++ rewrite,
# whose Access::Access() does an unconditional
# CHECK(selinux_status_open(true) >= 0) -- the is_selinux_enabled() guard the
# old C service_manager.c had is gone. Without selinuxfs it aborts on every
# start, so /dev/vndbinder never gets a context manager,
# vendor.qti.hardware.display.composer waits on it, init SIGKILLs it after 1s
# and restarts it forever. unity-system-compositor then waits 60s for a
# hwcomposer that can never appear and lightdm exits 1: black screen.
#
# Cost: AppArmor is now the disabled one, so Ubuntu Touch app confinement is
# off. 5.10 has no LSM stacking for two exclusive modules, so it is one or the
# other, and without SELinux there is no display at all.
CONFIG_LSM="lockdown,yama,loadpin,safesetid,integrity,selinux,smack,tomoyo,apparmor,bpf"
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_BOOTPARAM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_DEVELOP=y
